# What the three download pages name, and the one folder a deploy serves it
# from: `https://z-privacy.com/download/<file>`. Rule 81 — «يوم النشر يكون
# التنزيل من الموقع نفسه».
#
# Nothing in here is committed, and the reason is `dist/`'s reason one floor
# up: an archive is the output of a script run against a commit, and storing
# it beside the script stores the output of a function next to the function.
# The two files land here by hand on publishing day — the Linux bundle from
# `scripts/package_linux.sh` and the Windows installer from the Windows job —
# and `scripts/check_site_claims.py` then hashes each one and compares it with
# the fingerprint the pages print. Until they are here, the pages carry their
# «(final hashes on publishing day)» marker and the publishing run is red.
#
# The folder itself is tracked, by this file, so the deploy has somewhere to
# put them and nobody has to remember the path.
*
!.gitignore
